<zk>
	<div>
		<button id="btnReset" label="setValue(getValue())" onClick="drb.setValue(drb.getValue())"/>
		<button id="btnSetBegin" label="setBeginValue(Sep 1, 2025)"
			onClick="drb.setBeginValue(new java.util.GregorianCalendar(2025, 8, 1).getTime())"/>
		<button id="btnErrmsg" label="getErrorMessage()" onClick='errmsg.setValue("" + drb.getErrorMessage())'/>
		<button id="btnAppReject" label="throw WrongValueException"
			onClick='throw new org.zkoss.zk.ui.WrongValueException(drb, "Booked")'/>
		<button id="btnClearErr" label="clearErrorMessage()" onClick="drb.clearErrorMessage()"/>
		<label id="errmsg"/>
	</div>
	<div>
		<daterangebox id="drb" format="MMM d, yyyy" numberOfMonths="2"
			onChange='var e = event.getEnd();
				committedEnd.setValue(e == null ? "none" : String.valueOf(e.getTime()));'/>
	</div>
	<label id="committedEnd"/>
	<div>
		<daterangebox id="drbJira" width="330px" format="MMM d, yyyy" numberOfMonths="2"
			minNights="1" maxNights="14" allowEmpty="none"
			beginPlaceholder="Check-in" endPlaceholder="Check-out"
			onChange='jiraCommitted.setValue("committed")'/>
	</div>
	<label id="jiraCommitted"/>
	<label multiline="true">
		Steps to reproduce:
		1. Type "Sep 2, 2026" into begin, "Sep 4, 2025" into end (reversed), blur.

		- Expected: the errorbox names the reversed range AND both inputs still
			show what was typed, so the user can correct the year instead of
			retyping the pair.
		- Bug: the end input was wiped by the server snap-back, leaving an empty
			field plus an error about an entry no longer on screen.

		Guards, after step 1:
		- Correct the begin year to 2025 and blur: the pair on screen commits, so the
			label below the box shows an end value, not "none".
		- A redraw keeps both entries and the errorbox, also after a constraint change.
		- "setValue(getValue())": the box shows the server's range again, without
			the invalid mark.
		- "setBeginValue": only begin is replaced; the end keeps its rejected entry
			and the mark.
		- "getErrorMessage()" shows the rejection, and "null" after "setValue(getValue())".
		- "throw WrongValueException": "getErrorMessage()" shows "Booked", and
			"clearErrorMessage()" removes the mark.

		2. Open the calendar and pick a later day first, then an earlier day.

		- Expected: the two days commit as one range with the earlier day as the
			begin; a calendar pick carries no order, unlike typed input.

		3. Click "throw WrongValueException", then open the calendar and click Clear.

		- Expected: "getErrorMessage()" shows "null".

		4. In the second box (the Jira setup), type "Sep 2, 2026" into begin and blur,
			then "Sep 4, 2025" into end and blur.

		- Expected: the reversed range is rejected and both entries stay as typed;
			correcting the end year to 2026 commits the range.
	</label>
</zk>
